Request a 64-byte capture pitch so the GPU can import the frame

Stock mpv on the GPU path (--vo=gpu --hwdec=vaapi) showed nothing for an
852x480 H.264 stream. It decoded in hardware, then failed to map every
frame and stalled:

  MESA: error: panfrost: rejecting image due to unsupported offset or
        stride alignment.
  [vo/gpu/vaapi] Failed to import surface in EGL: 12291
  [vo/gpu] Mapping hardware decoded surface failed.

mpv imports NV12 one plane at a time, luma as R8 and chroma as GR88.
Panfrost on Bifrost (v7) needs those linear imports 64-byte aligned in
pitch and offset; only a planar NV12 import gets the looser 16. Mesa 25.0.7
(pan_layout.c, format_minimum_alignment) and 26.1.6
(pan_linear_or_tiled_row_align_req) are the same here, so a newer Mesa
does not help. cedrus gives the smallest pitch it can, ALIGN(width, 32)
since kernel patch 0125. That is 864 bytes for 852, which is 64-aligned
for 640, 960, 1280 and 1920 and not for 352, 720 or 852.

So ask for ALIGN(width, 64) when setting an NV12/NV21 CAPTURE format.
cedrus honours a larger bytesperline (kernel 0125 clamps the request
between ALIGN(width, 32) and its maximum). A driver that does not honour
it overwrites the field, and the G_FMT that follows is what describes the
surfaces either way. The chroma offset is pitch x a 16-aligned height, so
it is 64-aligned too. Widths that were already 64-aligned are unchanged.

---
diff --git a/src/v4l2.c b/src/v4l2.c
index ee43aed..cd87413 100644
--- a/src/v4l2.c
+++ b/src/v4l2.c
@@ -94,21 +94,38 @@ static void v4l2_setup_format(struct v4l2_format *format, unsigned int type,
 			      unsigned int pixelformat)
 {
 	unsigned int sizeimage;
+	unsigned int bytesperline = 0;
 
 	memset(format, 0, sizeof(*format));
 	format->type = type;
 
 	sizeimage = v4l2_type_is_output(type) ? SOURCE_SIZE_MAX : 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Ask for a capture pitch that is a multiple of 64 bytes. Panfrost
+	 * rejects any linear dma-buf plane imported as R8 or GR88 -- which is
+	 * how mpv and GStreamer bring NV12 into GL -- whose pitch or offset is
+	 * not 64-byte aligned ("rejecting image due to unsupported offset or
+	 * stride alignment"), in Mesa 25.0 and 26.1 alike. cedrus's minimum is
+	 * ALIGN(width, 32), so an 852-wide stream got an 864-byte pitch and
+	 * never reached the screen. cedrus honours a larger request; a driver
+	 * that does not simply overwrites it, and G_FMT reports what was used.
+	 */
+	if (!v4l2_type_is_output(type) &&
+	    (pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12 || pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21))
+		bytesperline = (width + 63) & ~63U;
+
 	if (v4l2_type_is_mplane(type)) {
 		format->fmt.pix_mp.width = width;
 		format->fmt.pix_mp.height = height;
 		format->fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = sizeimage;
+		format->fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].bytesperline = bytesperline;
 		format->fmt.pix_mp.pixelformat = pixelformat;
 	} else {
 		format->fmt.pix.width = width;
 		format->fmt.pix.height = height;
 		format->fmt.pix.sizeimage = sizeimage;
+		format->fmt.pix.bytesperline = bytesperline;
 		format->fmt.pix.pixelformat = pixelformat;
 	}
 }
